<task id="025" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Task read tools: spaarke_list_tasks, spaarke_get_task</title>
    <phase>1 Read tools</phase>
    <gate>r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF surface over events read with the BFF identity plus a BFF-applied filter (FR-15 caller scope)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Thin adapters over task 006's IEventsCapability, whose must-not-leak proofs already exist</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Tasks/{List,Get}TaskTool.cs and the Tasks ledger partial</parallel-reason>
    <deps>006, 020</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, tenant-isolation, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add two read-only MCP tools over task 006's IEventsCapability: spaarke_list_tasks (the caller's to-dos/events with the GET /api/v1/events filters) and spaarke_get_task (GET /api/v1/events/{id}). Run as the caller; a caller never sees another user's private event.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in MCP tool handlers and the events (sprk_event) model.</role>
  <goal>Both tools call IEventsCapability with the request context, return what REST returns for the same caller (slimmed), and pass must-not-leak tests; 200 tasks fit under 64 KiB.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-07 (read half), FR-15, NFR-02. Task 006 extracted get/list/create/complete from Api/Events/EventEndpoints.cs (group /api/v1/events: GET "/" :105, GET "/{id}" :117) into Services/Events/IEventsCapability with frozen REST bytes and must-not-leak proofs (tests/integration/auth/Events/EventCallerScopeTests.cs). IEventDataverseService reads with the BFF identity plus a BFF-applied filter.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Tasks/ListTasksTool.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Tasks/GetTaskTool.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.Tasks.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/Tasks/TaskReadToolsContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/Tasks/TaskReadToolsMustNotLeakTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Events/IEventsCapability.cs (task 006)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/auth/Events/EventCallerScopeTests.cs (task 006)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/CompleteDecisionTool.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="006" status="pending">Events capability and caller-scope proofs</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">General McpToolResults, ledger partials</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Run as the caller (IHttpContextAccessor; UserContextRequired; no app-only fallback). The tools call IEventsCapability only, never IEventDataverseService directly, and add no filter of their own (spec MUST NOT copy authorization).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">[McpArea("legal-operations")], readOnlyHint true, destructiveHint false, idempotentHint true, a title, description ≤ 1,024 characters ("to-dos and tasks (Spaarke events)"; not calendar meetings). Ledger rows in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.Tasks.cs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Slim rows: id, subject, due date, status, priority, regarding record name, open link; no description body in model-visible text. 200 tasks &lt; 64 KiB. Logs: tool name, latency, row count, outcome, correlation id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress.</constraint>
  </constraints>

