  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the r1 gate, 006 and 020; read IEventsCapability and EventCallerScopeTests.</step>
    <step order="2">Write the two tools and ledger rows; write contract and must-not-leak tests (reuse 006's seeded users and events).</step>
    <step order="3">Run MCP suites, ArchTests, conformance and the events contract tests; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="4">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="5">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a must-not-leak test fails through the capability (not the tool), STOP and report it as a found security defect in 006's capability; fix there with uac-r2 review.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>IEventsCapability (task 006) extracted from EventEndpoints statics; notes/reuse-scan.md row "Tasks (events)".</existing>
    <extension>The capability is reused unchanged; the tools are thin adapters on r1's host.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Copilot users cannot see their Spaarke to-dos (FR-07 read half fails).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build; dotnet test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Tasks/ListTasksTool.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Tasks/GetTaskTool.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/Tasks/TaskReadToolsContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/Tasks/TaskReadToolsMustNotLeakTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">For the same caller and filters, list ids equal GET /api/v1/events; get equals GET /api/v1/events/{id} (slimmed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (must-not-leak): user B's private event never appears in A's list, and get on it returns a not-found isError.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no caller context returns UserContextRequired.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">200 tasks serialise under 64 KiB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Events REST contract tests from 006 pass unchanged; ArchTests and conformance pass; publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-07, FR-15. Two adversarial-verifier passes (tenant-isolation tag). uac-r2 reviews.</notes>

